---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
	title="Terms | Drone Max Wind"
	description="Terms for using Drone Max Wind. The calculator is informational. You remain responsible for every flight decision."
>
	<Header />
	<main class="page-wrap max-w-3xl py-16">
		<p class="font-mono text-caption uppercase tracking-wide text-mute">Terms</p>
		<h1 class="mt-3 text-display-lg font-semibold text-ink">Use of this site.</h1>
		<p class="mt-5 text-body">
			Drone Max Wind is a free, informational wind planning tool for consumer drones. By using
			the site you agree to these terms. This is not legal advice.
		</p>
		<h2 class="mt-10 text-display-sm font-semibold text-ink">The calculator is a planning aid.</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 text-body">
			GO, CAUTION, and NO GO are estimates from published model limits and Open-Meteo wind at
			10 m, 80 m, and 120 m. Weather can change. Local terrain, rotors, and gusts can differ from
			the model. You remain responsible for the decision to fly, visual line of sight, airspace,
			and all applicable rules, including FAA recreational or Part 107 requirements in the US.
		</p>
		<h2 class="mt-10 text-display-sm font-semibold text-ink">No affiliation.</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 text-body">
			Drone Max Wind is independent. We are not affiliated with DJI, Autel, Skydio, Holy Stone,
			Open-Meteo, or any aviation authority. Brand names are used only to identify models and
			published specs.
		</p>
		<h2 class="mt-10 text-display-sm font-semibold text-ink">Data and specs.</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 text-body">
			Manufacturer ratings are taken from public specifications where we can find them. Some
			limits are labeled as class estimates. Specs can change; check the maker if you need an
			official figure. We do not guarantee completeness or accuracy.
		</p>
		<h2 class="mt-10 text-display-sm font-semibold text-ink">Acceptable use.</h2>
		<p class="mt-3 text-body">
			Do not abuse the weather APIs, scrape the site in a way that degrades the service, or
			present this tool as an official aviation product. The site is provided as is, without
			warranty.
		</p>
		<p class="mt-8 text-sm text-mute">Last updated: August 2026.</p>
	</main>
	<Footer />
</Layout>
